00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.335 line:0%
- I think that it's
really important

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.570 line:0%
to point out Donald
Trump yesterday,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:07.173 line:0%
I heard him say that he
was tired of Joe Biden

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:10.477 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
talking about how
Russia has nuclear power

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.178 line:0%
and it is a nuclear force.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:15.315 line:0%
And it sounds like, you
know, when you say that,

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.283 line:0%
that you're scared and
president Trump said

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.319 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
you know what Joe
Biden should be saying,

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:23.056 line:0%
we are a nuclear power
and we know what to do.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.158 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
And that I think therein
lies the difference

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:28.962 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
is that Donald
Trump was no wimp.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.131 line:0%
He wasn't anyone who
just said you know,

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.400 line:0%
I wanna bring troops
home and avoid war.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.069 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
He built up the
defense department.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:39.205 line:0%
He built up America's power.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.741 line:0%
He used the power
with Soleimani.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:46.713 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
He was really able to
show an unpredictability

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.083 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
when it came to using
America's power,

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.518 line:0%
but he has his criteria.

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:55.422 line:0%
And this is I think, a
really important point.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:57.257 line:0%
What is best for the US?

00:00:57.257 --> 00:01:00.193
