00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.139 line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin
in joining me today

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.542 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
is the former US
ambassador to Germany,

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:18.011 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
as well as the former
acting Director

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:21.114 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
of National Intelligence
or these great

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.250 line:0%
at least great for now,

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.252 line:0%
United States of America and
my friend and Californian.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.621 line:0%
We're gonna have to get
into that, Rich Grenell.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.623 line:0%
Welcome back to
the Rubin report.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.458 line:0%
- Dave, thanks for having me.

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:32.959 line:0%
Always a pleasure.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.462 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
- Let's just do the California
thing quick in one minute.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
What the high hell are
you doing there still man.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.199 line:0%
- I love this place.

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.033 line:0%
I can't leave.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.434 line:0%
I can't abandon it.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.603 line:0%
It's bad.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.972 line:0%
Look, today's the
filing deadline

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.875 line:0%
for people running
for governor, senate,

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
congressional races,
all the races.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.913 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Doesn't look like we're gonna
have any major candidate

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.516 line:0%
running against Newsom.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.819 line:0%
And I think that's just more
of a commentary on the fact

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.387 line:0%
that the system here is broken.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.323 line:0%
They do mail-in ballots.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.425 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Democrats completely
rule this place

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.926 line:0%
like a third world country.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:11.831 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
And so therefore we really
don't have competition.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.135 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- You know, Rick, I
knew it was bad in Cali

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.704 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
When I was calling people
to say I was leaving.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.706 line:0%
And I thought you were
gonna be the one guy,

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:22.108 line:0%
because you were trying to
clean up the roles there.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.643 line:0%
And you're still trying to
do a whole bunch of stuff.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.478 line:0%
And I know how much
you love California.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.113 line:0%
You've been there forever,

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.882 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
but I was calling people
to say, I'm leaving.

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:30.049 line:0%
And everyone was like

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.384 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
oh great, you know,
you should go.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.153 line:0%
It's time to go get outta dodge.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.288 line:0%
And you were the only person

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.956 line:0%
I thought was gonna say stay,

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.958 line:0%
and you go, I get it.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.460 line:0%
And then I was like all
right, I'm outta here.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.928 line:0%
By the way Rick,

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.530 line:0%
every time I mention
California on the show,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.331 line:0%
I put money into to this jar.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.566 line:0%
And at the end of the year,

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.468 line:0%
I'm gonna be handing
a whole bunch of cash.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.870 line:0%
And I'm throwing in a couple
thousand dollars of my money

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
for somebody that's
willing to leave California

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.708 line:0%
and migrate to Florida.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.676 line:0%
So.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.911 line:0%
- I thought you were gonna say

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.647 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
for somebody who needs
to help pay taxes

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.515 line:0%
because they stayed there.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:04.584 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
And so I'll gladly
take the money.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:08.488 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
- No, I am not paying
your taxes to king Newsom.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.490 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
Okay, but let's
get onto the stuff

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
that I really wanted to
talk to you about this week

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.160 line:0%
because obviously
there's this whole

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.162 line:0%
Russia/Ukraine situation.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.898 line:0%
This is what you're
an expert it in,

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.234 line:0%
as an ambassador and on
the intelligence side

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.735 line:0%
and all of that.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.704 line:0%
So I thought maybe we could
start by just doing a little,

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:28.675 line:0%
a little 101 on what you think

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.944 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
American foreign
policy should be like.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.278 line:0%
So before we just jump into,

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.546 line:0%
before we get into the specifics

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.048 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
of what's happening
in Russia and Ukraine,

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:37.116 line:0%
just generally what you think

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.519 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
America's role in
the world should be,

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:43.022 line:0%
and maybe how it was
when you were working

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:43.990 line:0%
with that Orange guy

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.024 line:0%
versus how it is now,

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.259 line:0%
let's just start there

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.961 line:0%
and then we'll jump
to the specifics.

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.429 line:0%
- Yeah, look, you know,

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:52.765 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
I think that the America first
policy is a fantastic one

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.701 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and it doesn't
mean America alone.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:58.238 align:start position:0% line:0%
And it doesn't mean just simply
that we bring troops home

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:01.541 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and we ignore crises
around the world.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:04.877 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
I think what America
first means is just that,

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.646 line:0%
is that we put America first.

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:08.848 line:0%
We think about our
US National Security.

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:13.186 line:0%
That's the criteria, what is
good for US National Security,

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:16.689 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
but it also means that our
allies have to stand up

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.992 line:0%
and we encourage them to do so.

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:22.595 line:0%
So it's why we removed
our us troops in Somalia,

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.030 line:0%
'cause we said to Kenya,

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.833 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
hey, can you kind of police
your own neighborhood?

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:30.403 line:0%
It's why we wanted the
Europeans to do more.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.939 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
And I think there's
an admission,

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.842 line:0%
a tacit admission from
the Germans right now

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.810 line:0%
in terms of their policy,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.814 line:0%
that they believe that
they on the wrong track

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.284 line:0%
for 10, 16 years of Merkel.

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:47.654 line:0%
They now are completely flipped.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.722 line:0%
They're better than
the Senate Democrats.

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.991 line:0%
They're better than Joe Biden

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:54.160 line:0%
because there's an admission now

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.197 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
that wow, not paying your
NATO fair share of 2%

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.265 line:0%
was a huge mistake.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.167 line:0%
So what did the Germans do?

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.635 line:0%
They decided to say

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:06.272 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
we're gonna pay it all at
once in one year to catch up.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.974 line:0%
This is a huge admission

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:10.677 line:0%
that they have been on the
wrong track for 16 years.

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.178 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Then they turn
around and they say

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:14.747 line:0%
we gotta stop this
Russian pipeline.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.049 line:0%
This is historic.

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.317 line:0%
This is unprecedented.

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:19.952 line:0%
Don't forget just
a few months ago,

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.788 line:0%
not very long ago,

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:24.390 line:0%
Senate Democrats, the
Biden administration,

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:27.126 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and the government of
chancellor Merkel in Germany

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:32.131 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
all came together to say
drop the sanctions on Putin,

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.134 line:0%
on the Russian Nord
Stream 2 pipeline

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:39.405 line:0%
because they all said
this may encourage him.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:43.343 line:0%
If we squeeze him too much,
then he's gonna of lash out.

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:46.179 line:0%
Well, obviously they were wrong

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:49.449 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and they completely
got it upended.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:53.086 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
And so the sanctions
should have been put on,

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:55.021 line:0%
or stayed on we should say,

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.824 line:0%
but the Democrats, the
Biden administration

00:05:57.824 --> 00:06:00.626 line:0%
should have kept
that pressure on.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
And I think that we'd
have a different scenario,

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:06.232 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
but when Putin is
looking at Afghanistan

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:09.168 line:0%
and by the way, if people
are not talking enough

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:13.172 line:0%
about the policy that
Biden put in place

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:17.210 line:0%
to drop the Houthis from
the terrorist watch list.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.711 line:0%
As soon as they did that Dave,

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:21.114 line:0%
we had a couple of months later,

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:22.715 line:0%
what did the Houthis do?

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:25.551 line:0%
They were bombarding the UAE.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:28.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
Abu Dhabi was receiving
missiles from the Houthis.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:33.259 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Now this was by official
Washington, largely ignored.

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:35.361 line:0%
There wasn't a correlation made

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:36.729 line:0%
between hey you know,

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.464 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Joe Biden and the
Biden administration,

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.233 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
all the Democrats
just took the Houthis

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.734 line:0%
off the terrorist list,

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:42.935 line:0%
and what happened?

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:44.637 line:0%
They started acting
like terrorists.

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:49.642 line:0%
And so you literally have
to push official Washington

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:55.448 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
to see that these weak
policies translate globally

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.918 line:0%
into terrible situations.

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:00.319 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
I don't think it's
too much to say

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:03.656 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
that Joe Biden's
weakness is causing war.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:06.659 line:0%
It's scandal, destruction,

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:09.595 line:0%
and we have to be able to
shake the Senate Democrats

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:12.298 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
because the Germans
now see that.

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:14.834 line:0%
And it's, I never thought
I would see it in my day.

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:17.103 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
And they're certainly not
saying Rick Grenell was right,

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:18.571 line:0%
Donald Trump was right,

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:20.039 line:0%
but they're coming awful close.

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:22.775 align:start position:0% line:0%
- So let's stick with that
Germany situation for a minute,

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:25.278 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
because so you were ambassador
to Germany under Trump.

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:28.414 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
And if you listen to the
media throughout all of that,

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:32.251 line:0%
you know, Trump was mean and
scaring people all the time

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:35.221 line:0%
and you went in there and you
weren't listening to anybody.

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:37.390 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
And the other ambassador
wasn't happy with you

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.624 line:0%
and all of this stuff.

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:41.561 line:0%
However things were
basically working

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:44.030 line:0%
in terms of all of our
international agreements.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:46.999 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
And we were at least
trying to encourage people

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.634 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
to pay a bit more,
which as you just said

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.636 line:0%
now they're catching up with,

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:53.906 line:0%
did everything shift
overnight basically,

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:56.075 line:0%
once Biden took over?

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.046 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- I think that there's
a combination of
once Biden took over

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:01.314 line:0%
and once Merkel was gone,

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.082 line:0%
it was relatively
at the same time.

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:06.419 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
And you know, Merkelism
really didn't work.

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:07.720 line:0%
We had 16 years of,

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:11.023 line:0%
and I'm passionate
about this subject

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:13.593 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
is that I believe
that chancellor Merkel

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:17.263 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
in making her policy
Germany first,

00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:22.268 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
she decided to move the German
trans-Atlantic relationship

00:08:23.603 --> 00:08:25.071 line:0%
away from the west

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:27.540 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
instead of making a
Western facing Alliance

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.076 line:0%
where you stand with the
west and you do things

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:32.445 line:0%
that benefit the west.

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:35.481 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
She decided to have a foreign
policy like Switzerland

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:38.217 line:0%
and be everybody's friend
and to sell cars, you know,

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:41.521 line:0%
in Moscow and Beijing and
Teran and everywhere else.

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:45.925 line:0%
And don't forget when
I arrived in Germany,

00:08:45.925 --> 00:08:47.793 line:0%
I was walking around one day

00:08:47.793 --> 00:08:52.498 line:0%
and I walked past this
hotel youth hostile,

00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:54.433 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and I looked over
and it was literally,

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:56.002 line:0%
I'm not exaggerating,

00:08:56.002 --> 00:09:00.106 line:0%
the property of North Korea
in the middle of Berlin.

00:09:00.106 --> 00:09:01.974 line:0%
And I went back to the
embassy and I was like

00:09:01.974 --> 00:09:03.142 line:0%
what the hell?

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.946 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
There's a north Korean
hotel youth hostile

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:08.180 line:0%
in the middle of Berlin.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.449 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
I mean, they're under
international sanctions.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:11.784 line:0%
This is illegal.

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:13.019 line:0%
And they're, and you know,

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:14.820 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
everybody at the state
department was like

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.055 line:0%
yeah, but I guess we've
allowed that to happen.

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:18.090 line:0%
No and I said, no,
no, no, no guessing,

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.325 line:0%
this is unacceptable.

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:21.394 line:0%
So I took it to
chancellor Merkel

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:23.162 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and you know there
were a lot of excuses,

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:24.764 line:0%
oh, it's not really us.

00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:26.432 line:0%
It's this management company.

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:27.700 line:0%
And I said, I don't care.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.569 line:0%
It's in the middle of
Berlin, shut it down.

00:09:29.569 --> 00:09:32.872 line:0%
You're violating UN sanctions.

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:34.473 line:0%
They eventually shut it down.

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:37.543 line:0%
They weren't happy with
me for pointing that out,

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:38.778 line:0%
but I wasn't happy with them

00:09:38.778 --> 00:09:41.314 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
for violating
international sanctions.

00:09:41.314 --> 00:09:43.950 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
My point in telling you
this is that they've moved

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.786 line:0%
away from the west for 16 years

00:09:46.786 --> 00:09:49.589 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
while the German Marshall
fund has just applauded them

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:53.593 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
as you know, this
great economic power.

00:09:53.593 --> 00:09:56.128 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
And yet I think
that a difference.

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.497 line:0%
You can bifurcate the
trans-Atlantic Alliance

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:02.602 align:start position:0% line:0%
from the Western facing
Alliance, the Western Alliance,

00:10:02.602 --> 00:10:05.771 line:0%
and Merkel decided to just
be a part of this you know,

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:07.807 line:0%
trans-Atlantic Alliance,

00:10:07.807 --> 00:10:09.575 line:0%
which was not Western facing.

00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:12.411 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
She's the one who moved
Germany and Europe

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:14.046 line:0%
away from the west.

00:10:14.046 --> 00:10:16.449 line:0%
And now I think they're
scrambling to say yikes,

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.152 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
I think we might have
encouraged war in Ukraine.

00:10:20.152 --> 00:10:23.422 line:0%
- Okay, so with all
of that in mind,

00:10:23.422 --> 00:10:26.025 line:0%
none of this happened
for the four years

00:10:26.025 --> 00:10:27.693 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
under the guy that
you worked for.

00:10:27.693 --> 00:10:30.963 line:0%
And everyone kept saying oh,
but Trump is Putin's puppet

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:32.365 line:0%
and all of these things.

00:10:32.365 --> 00:10:35.568 line:0%
And yet oddly Putin
made a move on Crimea

00:10:35.568 --> 00:10:37.670 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
when Joe Biden was
vice president,

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:39.372 line:0%
and then he cooled
it off for four years

00:10:39.372 --> 00:10:42.341 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
and then made a move
when Biden was president.

00:10:42.341 --> 00:10:43.809 line:0%
Are any of these
things connected

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:45.845 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
or am I a crazy
conspiracy theorist here?

00:10:47.079 --> 00:10:47.913 line:0%
- I know you personally,

00:10:47.913 --> 00:10:49.348 line:0%
you're not crazy,

00:10:49.348 --> 00:10:51.884 align:start position:0% line:0%
but don't forget that we
should also put in there though

00:10:51.884 --> 00:10:55.755 line:0%
that Putin moved on
George, under Bush,

00:10:55.755 --> 00:10:57.256 line:0%
under President Bush.

00:10:57.256 --> 00:10:58.958 line:0%
This is not a partisan statement

00:10:58.958 --> 00:11:03.295 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
to say that you've got to
be able to put America first

00:11:03.295 --> 00:11:08.100 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and articulate the responses
of the US government.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.335 line:0%
And you know,

00:11:09.335 --> 00:11:11.404 line:0%
I think that it's really
important to point out

00:11:11.404 --> 00:11:14.640 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
Donald Trump yesterday,
I heard him say

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:17.243 line:0%
that he was tired of
Joe Biden talking about

00:11:17.243 --> 00:11:21.013 line:0%
how Russia has nuclear power
and it is a nuclear force.

00:11:21.013 --> 00:11:24.583 line:0%
And it sounds like you
know, when you say that,

00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:25.484 line:0%
that you're scared,

00:11:25.484 --> 00:11:26.652 line:0%
and president Trump said

00:11:26.652 --> 00:11:28.587 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
you know what Joe
Biden should be saying,

00:11:28.587 --> 00:11:32.324 line:0%
we are a nuclear power
and we know what to do.

00:11:32.324 --> 00:11:34.427 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
And that I think therein
lies the difference

00:11:34.427 --> 00:11:38.230 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
is that Donald
Trump was no wimp.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.433 line:0%
He wasn't anyone who
just said you know,

00:11:40.433 --> 00:11:42.668 line:0%
I wanna bring troops
home and avoid war.

00:11:42.668 --> 00:11:45.371 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
He built up the
defense department,

00:11:45.371 --> 00:11:48.474 line:0%
he built up America's power.

00:11:48.474 --> 00:11:50.976 line:0%
He used the power
with Soleimani.

00:11:50.976 --> 00:11:53.579 line:0%
He was really able to,

00:11:53.579 --> 00:11:56.716 line:0%
to show an unpredictability

00:11:56.716 --> 00:11:59.452 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
when it came to using
America's power,

00:11:59.452 --> 00:12:02.221 line:0%
but he has his criteria.

00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:04.590 line:0%
And this is I think, a
really important point.

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:07.093 line:0%
What is best for the US?

00:12:07.093 --> 00:12:08.694 line:0%
And I'll finish by
saying, you know,

00:12:08.694 --> 00:12:11.130 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
the state department
needs to learn this lesson

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:14.300 line:0%
because when you talk
about America first

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.736 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and all of the great things
about what that means

00:12:16.736 --> 00:12:19.271 line:0%
to be an America first advocate,

00:12:19.271 --> 00:12:21.841 line:0%
it doesn't mean America alone.

00:12:21.841 --> 00:12:24.877 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
And there's a way to
articulate America first.

00:12:24.877 --> 00:12:26.579 line:0%
And I believe this passionately,

00:12:26.579 --> 00:12:30.015 line:0%
that America first helps
our allies and others.

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:32.084 line:0%
When America is out front,

00:12:32.084 --> 00:12:36.522 line:0%
trying to push forward
democracy, human rights,

00:12:36.522 --> 00:12:37.990 line:0%
the rule of law, guess what?

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:39.959 line:0%
Every economy benefits,

00:12:39.959 --> 00:12:42.828 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
we see that, inflation
is spiky now,

00:12:42.828 --> 00:12:44.463 line:0%
economies are not doing well.

00:12:44.463 --> 00:12:46.332 line:0%
When America puts itself first,

00:12:46.332 --> 00:12:49.435 line:0%
capitalism and the
rule of law thrive,

00:12:49.435 --> 00:12:51.937 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
that brings up
every other country.

00:12:51.937 --> 00:12:55.674 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
We should have state
depart ambassadors overseas

00:12:55.674 --> 00:13:00.246 line:0%
who articulate why an America
first policy is good for them.

00:13:00.246 --> 00:13:02.815 line:0%
There should be no
apologies about this.

00:13:02.815 --> 00:13:04.517 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
It's better to
have America first

00:13:04.517 --> 00:13:07.586 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
than to allow Russia or China
to put themselves first.

00:13:07.586 --> 00:13:10.456 line:0%
And I think what we've seen
from 16 years of Merkel,

00:13:10.456 --> 00:13:12.858 line:0%
it's much better
for America first

00:13:12.858 --> 00:13:14.326 line:0%
than to put Germany first.

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:18.864 line:0%
- So who do you think Biden
is putting first right now?

00:13:18.864 --> 00:13:20.499 line:0%
I mean, we, it seems
like a lifetime ago,

00:13:20.499 --> 00:13:22.101 line:0%
but literally only
three weeks ago,

00:13:22.101 --> 00:13:23.936 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
right before this
whole thing started.

00:13:23.936 --> 00:13:26.605 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
We had about a two week window
of every day where Biden,

00:13:26.605 --> 00:13:29.875 align:start position:0% line:0%
it sounded like he was basically
acting as Putin's PR guy.

00:13:29.875 --> 00:13:31.944 line:0%
He kept being like well,
he's probably gonna go,

00:13:31.944 --> 00:13:33.212 line:0%
maybe he'll go.

00:13:33.212 --> 00:13:35.314 line:0%
These are the 16 things
we don't want him to do.

00:13:35.314 --> 00:13:37.149 line:0%
Here's a bunch of
stuff he can do.

00:13:37.149 --> 00:13:39.451 line:0%
I mean, what is our policy

00:13:39.451 --> 00:13:41.086 line:0%
at this point?

00:13:41.086 --> 00:13:44.156 line:0%
- Look, I don't wanna
get too philosophical,

00:13:44.156 --> 00:13:45.558 line:0%
or theoretical here,

00:13:45.558 --> 00:13:48.394 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
but the opposite of
America first is consensus,

00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:51.030 line:0%
especially consensus
with the Europeans.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:52.932 line:0%
And I spent eight
years at the UN

00:13:52.932 --> 00:13:54.967 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
and I can tell you inside
the security council,

00:13:54.967 --> 00:13:56.268 line:0%
that any time there's
a policy or a statement

00:13:56.268 --> 00:13:59.972 line:0%
coming out of the
security council,

00:13:59.972 --> 00:14:00.906 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
it's the lowest
common denominator

00:14:00.906 --> 00:14:02.074 line:0%
of what 15 countries believe.

00:14:02.074 --> 00:14:05.978 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
And it's not putting
America first,

00:14:05.978 --> 00:14:09.081 line:0%
certainly not putting
democracy human rights,

00:14:09.081 --> 00:14:10.616 line:0%
the rule of law first.

00:14:10.616 --> 00:14:14.920 line:0%
And so Joe Biden is trapped
in official Washington ideas

00:14:16.121 --> 00:14:19.358 line:0%
that he wants to be
loved by the world.

00:14:19.358 --> 00:14:20.359 line:0%
He talks like you know,

00:14:20.359 --> 00:14:22.027 line:0%
I know all these world leaders.

00:14:22.027 --> 00:14:27.032 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
He really prioritizes the
applause from the globalists.

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:29.501 line:0%
And so when you think about it,

00:14:29.501 --> 00:14:33.439 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
he really wants the
Europeans to be pleased.

00:14:33.439 --> 00:14:36.175 line:0%
The reason he dropped the
sanctions on Nord Stream 2

00:14:36.175 --> 00:14:39.511 align:start position:0% line:0%
is 'cause Merkel and the Germans
at the time asked him to.

00:14:39.511 --> 00:14:42.348 line:0%
He maximized being
with the Germans,

00:14:42.348 --> 00:14:45.584 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
being with the Europeans,
having them love him.

00:14:45.584 --> 00:14:48.554 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Look no further
than the Iran deal.

00:14:48.554 --> 00:14:50.623 line:0%
Iran deal two.

00:14:50.623 --> 00:14:53.392 line:0%
And now we see the
Europeans saying

00:14:53.392 --> 00:14:55.094 line:0%
wait a minute, this deal,

00:14:55.094 --> 00:14:56.795 line:0%
we're gonna have
to put it on ice

00:14:56.795 --> 00:14:58.631 line:0%
because it's going south.

00:14:58.631 --> 00:15:01.300 line:0%
When the Europeans are saying

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:03.569 line:0%
we need to stop this process,

00:15:03.569 --> 00:15:07.973 line:0%
And the Biden team is not
the one calling it first,

00:15:07.973 --> 00:15:11.076 line:0%
we've got a big problem when
you're behind the Europeans,

00:15:11.076 --> 00:15:12.411 line:0%
but this is the policy.

00:15:12.411 --> 00:15:14.146 line:0%
Now I can go through you know,

00:15:14.146 --> 00:15:15.848 line:0%
each area of the world.

00:15:15.848 --> 00:15:18.017 line:0%
Look at Venezuela policy now.

00:15:18.017 --> 00:15:22.521 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
We're moving and transitioning
into engagement again,

00:15:22.521 --> 00:15:24.590 line:0%
which already failed
with the Venezuelan

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.926 line:0%
simply because there's a
bunch of Latin countries

00:15:26.926 --> 00:15:28.360 line:0%
that want us to do that.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.296 line:0%
And Joe Biden is leaning in

00:15:30.296 --> 00:15:32.631 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and letting them
determine that policy.

00:15:32.631 --> 00:15:34.400 line:0%
The same thing in the Balkans.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.635 line:0%
I worked very hard
on cost of Serbia.

00:15:36.635 --> 00:15:38.704 line:0%
We had four economic agreements.

00:15:38.704 --> 00:15:40.673 line:0%
You know what the policy is now,

00:15:40.673 --> 00:15:43.509 line:0%
let the Europeans
lead on this issue.

00:15:43.509 --> 00:15:45.811 line:0%
And you know, this is
the whole 1990s crowd

00:15:45.811 --> 00:15:48.981 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
filled with NGOs that
loved to write white papers

00:15:48.981 --> 00:15:51.116 line:0%
and tell rich people
to give them money

00:15:51.116 --> 00:15:52.351 line:0%
to think about these issues.

00:15:52.351 --> 00:15:54.653 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
But they're not
making sense at all.

00:15:54.653 --> 00:15:56.155 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
- Do you think
that these people,

00:15:56.155 --> 00:15:59.058 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
without getting too far
into the philosophical part,

00:15:59.058 --> 00:15:59.892 line:0%
then do you think that,

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.328 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
that he at least has
competent people?

00:16:02.328 --> 00:16:04.196 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I mean when you listen
to Kamala Harris

00:16:04.196 --> 00:16:05.998 line:0%
talk about this stuff, you know,

00:16:05.998 --> 00:16:07.533 line:0%
Ukraine is small.

00:16:07.533 --> 00:16:09.068 line:0%
Russia is big.

00:16:09.068 --> 00:16:10.302 line:0%
Even Tony Blinken,

00:16:10.302 --> 00:16:13.505 line:0%
I mean, all of, they
don't competent to me.

00:16:13.505 --> 00:16:16.875 line:0%
Putting aside that you may have
a philosophical disagreement

00:16:16.875 --> 00:16:19.244 line:0%
with them on what US
strengths should be

00:16:19.244 --> 00:16:20.479 line:0%
or something like that.

00:16:20.479 --> 00:16:21.714 line:0%
Do they strike you
as competent people?

00:16:21.714 --> 00:16:25.284 line:0%
- But a friend in need
is a friend indeed Dave.

00:16:25.284 --> 00:16:28.053 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
And look, you know,
they're not competent.

00:16:28.053 --> 00:16:30.689 line:0%
And I blame the Sacramento media

00:16:30.689 --> 00:16:34.326 line:0%
for allowing Kamala
Harris as a woman

00:16:34.326 --> 00:16:37.796 line:0%
and as a black person to rise

00:16:37.796 --> 00:16:40.833 line:0%
and win all of these
different offices,

00:16:40.833 --> 00:16:42.468 line:0%
simply because of her identity.

00:16:42.468 --> 00:16:44.103 line:0%
She wasn't qualified.

00:16:44.103 --> 00:16:45.371 line:0%
She doesn't have the capacity.

00:16:45.371 --> 00:16:47.906 line:0%
And I honestly will
double down on that.

00:16:47.906 --> 00:16:49.174 line:0%
If you look,

00:16:49.174 --> 00:16:51.510 line:0%
there's no possible way,
Susan Rice and Ron Klain

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:55.214 line:0%
did not prepare her
with a good book

00:16:55.214 --> 00:16:58.117 line:0%
of what to say and what to
do and what the policy was.

00:16:58.117 --> 00:17:00.719 line:0%
I don't think it was
a lack of preparation.

00:17:00.719 --> 00:17:02.821 line:0%
I think it is a capacity issue

00:17:02.821 --> 00:17:05.391 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
that she doesn't
understand these issues.

00:17:05.391 --> 00:17:08.460 line:0%
She's been allowed
to rise to the top

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.429 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
without any vetting
from the media.

00:17:10.429 --> 00:17:14.700 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
There's been no push until
she got into the presidential,

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.302 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and then the national media
a little bit were like

00:17:17.302 --> 00:17:18.771 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
wait a minute, you're
not really ready.

00:17:18.771 --> 00:17:20.205 line:0%
And so she imploded,

00:17:20.205 --> 00:17:23.042 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
but the Sacramento media
allowed her just to you know,

00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:24.910 line:0%
catapult and take over.

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:26.645 line:0%
I don't think she's qualified.

00:17:26.645 --> 00:17:29.281 line:0%
I think Anthony Blinken
should have been fired

00:17:29.281 --> 00:17:30.983 line:0%
after Afghanistan.

00:17:30.983 --> 00:17:33.052 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I don't understand
why he's still around.

00:17:33.052 --> 00:17:34.686 line:0%
He's totally weak.

00:17:34.686 --> 00:17:37.089 line:0%
Wendy Sherman, the deputy
at the state department,

00:17:37.089 --> 00:17:38.991 line:0%
you know, her nickname is
what do you want Wendy.

00:17:38.991 --> 00:17:41.093 line:0%
When she goes into negotiations,

00:17:41.093 --> 00:17:42.561 line:0%
she gives away the store.

00:17:42.561 --> 00:17:45.097 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
She did it in North Korea,
in Iran, with Russia.

00:17:45.097 --> 00:17:48.233 line:0%
I don't know how many times
we're gonna put her forward.

00:17:48.233 --> 00:17:50.903 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
She's the terrible negotiator
for the United States.

00:17:50.903 --> 00:17:54.139 line:0%
And then, you know, Susan
Rice is behind the scenes

00:17:54.139 --> 00:17:56.075 line:0%
supposedly doing
domestic policy,

00:17:56.075 --> 00:17:58.377 line:0%
which she's not qualified for.

00:17:58.377 --> 00:18:00.312 line:0%
But I think she's
pulling the string

00:18:00.312 --> 00:18:02.448 line:0%
of all of these other positions.

00:18:02.448 --> 00:18:04.016 line:0%
Remember Susan Rice,

00:18:04.016 --> 00:18:06.018 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
when she was national
security advisor,

00:18:06.018 --> 00:18:08.554 line:0%
had two deputies at the NSC.

00:18:08.554 --> 00:18:09.988 line:0%
One was Avril Haine,

00:18:09.988 --> 00:18:12.925 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
who runs the intelligence
program as DNI,

00:18:12.925 --> 00:18:14.860 line:0%
and the other was
Anthony Blinken.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:16.762 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Who's now running
the state department.

00:18:16.762 --> 00:18:18.730 line:0%
So diplomacy and intelligence

00:18:19.598 --> 00:18:21.133 line:0%
all are really under Susan Rice.

00:18:21.133 --> 00:18:22.267 line:0%
They're her deputies.

00:18:22.267 --> 00:18:23.735 line:0%
She chose them.

